# Prompt
SVI File Format

It is a markdown-syntax file with the following sections:

Section 'Destination File'
Target file name with generated code, e.g. code.js
The parameter is optional in cases when *.svi file is a reusable piece of prompt, not a final
prompt for code generation
Section 'Input parameters'
e.g. class Storage from utils/storage.js
It should describe input parameters to tell AI which imports from other modules are necessary.
Section 'Output'
It should describe what is exported outside module that other modules should know
Section 'Options'
ProgrammingLanguage=Node.js - optional, programming language may be taken from the global svi.json config file
Active=True
Section 'Import prompts'
<Paths to other svi files>
It can contain parths to reusable prompts in other *.svi files, that will be added to the final prompt
Section 'Prompt'
The prompt itself, it should describe the code of the file so that it will be generated by AI
with satisfactory level of determination according to chosen LLM model.
If results are flaky, you should choose another model or split file into several smaller ones.
